Figure 2 demonstrates the in vivo kinetics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, showing that after intramuscular injection, the Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 remains localized at the injection site with no detectable systemic distribution to internal organs over 21 days. The fluorescent signal at the injection site initially decreases rapidly, followed by a moderate increase around day 2, and then steadily declines, with approximately 20% of the original signal detected at day 21, indicating gradual clearance of the nanoparticles.